  "details": "When using HTC Vive controllers while having the advanced settings option on, whenever we move or turn using the touchpad, we get the emote associated with the position of the touchpad where our finger was when we released.\nI find it annoying that whenever i jump or stop walking my avatar ends up with a surprised face, or when i turn i stick my toungue up, for example.\nI want to use advanced settings because i like not having to have my finger over the touchpad to hold an emote, but i dont want to have an emote whenever i finish moving, it is cumbersome.\nThis didnt happen before the IK/3.0 update.",
